<title>USA: Dow gains more than 50 points.</title>
<headline>Dow gains more than 50 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average gained more than 50 points Monday, lifting the barometer of 30 blue-chip stocks above 6,000 points for the first time in nearly a week amid moderate economic growth and subdued inflation.</p>
<p>Shortly  after 2 p.m., the Dow rose 50.31 points to 6,019.69, which activated the New York Stock Exchange's limits on program trading.</p>
